    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q14a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $n^3$ is even if and only if $n$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is even, its cube is even. If $n$ is odd, its cube is odd; by contraposition, an even cube requires an even $n$. Hence the equivalence holds.",
          "worked": "Let $n\\in\\mathbb Z$. If $n$ is even, write $n=2k$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n^3&=8k^3\\\\n^3&=2(4k^3).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $n^3$ is even.\n\nFor the reverse direction, prove the contrapositive. If $n$ is odd, write $n=2k+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n^3&=8k^3+12k^2+6k+1\\\\n^3&=2(4k^3+6k^2+3k)+1.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $n^3$ is odd. Consequently, if $n^3$ is even, $n$ is even. Both directions establish the result.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q14b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, prove that $\\sqrt[3]{2}$ is irrational.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt[3]{2}$ is irrational.\n\nA fraction in lowest terms would force both its numerator and denominator to be even, contradicting lowest terms.",
          "worked": "Suppose $\\sqrt[3]{2}$ is rational. Write $\\sqrt[3]{2}=\\frac{m}{n}$ in lowest terms, where $m,n\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $n\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{m^3}{n^3}&=2\\\\m^3&=2n^3.\\end{align*}$$\nBy part (a), $m$ is even. Put $m=2k$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2k)^3&=2n^3\\\\8k^3&=2n^3\\\\n^3&=4k^3.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $n^3$ is even, so part (a) shows that $n$ is even. Both $m$ and $n$ have the common factor $2$, contradicting lowest terms. Therefore $\\sqrt[3]{2}$ is irrational.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      }
    ]
  },
